From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muthukumar <muthukumardce@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Apr 2026 14:14:03 +0530
Subject: Fix Cr144 typed array API migration in fingerprint noise patches
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Chromium 144 migrated DOMFloat32Array/DOMUint8Array from raw pointer
access (Data()/length()) to base::span (AsSpan()/size()). This broke
the fingerprint noise injection in WebAudio and WebGL patches that were
written against the older API.

Changes:
- webaudio/analyser_node.cc: Migrate getFloatFrequencyData,
  getByteFrequencyData, getFloatTimeDomainData, getByteTimeDomainData
  noise loops from array->Data()/length() to array->AsSpan()/size()
- webaudio/audio_buffer.cc: Migrate getChannelData noise loop
- webaudio/offline_audio_context.cc: Migrate FireCompletionEvent
  rendered buffer noise loop
- webgl/webgl2_rendering_context_base.cc: Migrate getBufferSubData
  and both readPixels overloads from raw uint8_t* to base::span;
  add missing #include "base/containers/span.h"
- webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc: Migrate readPixels noise
  loop; add missing #include "base/containers/span.h"

All noise logic unchanged — only the buffer access pattern updated
to match Cr144 Blink typed array API.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

